A Dma its pool's destroy takes stays in the channel table.
The table would name freed memory, and the channel could never be bound again;
the table names only live Dmas.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: dma channel table names a dma that is gone
Witness: fuzz dma-dies-with-pool

diff --git a/kernel/dma.c b/kernel/dma.c
--- a/kernel/dma.c
+++ b/kernel/dma.c
@@ -58,7 +58,6 @@ void dma_drop(struct cap *end)
 void dma_forget(struct dma *d)
 {
     dmac_halt(d->channel);
-    channel_dma[d->channel - DMA_FIRST] = 0;
 }
 
 #if DMA_FAKE
